{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3447","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3447","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3447\",\"parent_revision\":\"9f3469213f7a3d7e24e77dc55fd8369a6bb2ba4765df099dbba96c189d26857d\",\"root_revision\":\"9f3469213f7a3d7e24e77dc55fd8369a6bb2ba4765df099dbba96c189d26857d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nplugin-creator now states the portability rule inline in every skill and agent that writes or reviews runtime text (commit c0858ca on `worktree-melodic-plotting-emerson`), but several of its own runtime files fail that rule in forms `skills/lint/scripts/audit_runtime_escapes.py` does not detect. Found during the code review of dab51da; each is pre-existing, not introduced by that commit.\\n\\nRepo-rooted or authoring-repo paths in runtime text, undetected because they are backticked prose or a bare command rather than a markdown link, and `scripts`/`docs` are outside `_REPO_ROOT_DIRS`:\\n\\n- `skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md:222` \u2014 `uv run plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/create_plugin.py` (an installed consumer has no `plugins/` tree; the scanner skips it as same-plugin).\\n- `skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md:338-340` \u2014 backticked `../../../../plan/architect-plugin-lifecycle.md` and `../../CLAUDE.md`.\\n- `skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md:406` \u2014 `.claude/rules/uv-run-fallback.md`.\\n- `skills/optimize-claude-md/SKILL.md:97,101` \u2014 `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/references/...` in prose; `skills/component-patterns/SKILL.md:158` \u2014 `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/`; `skills/lint/SKILL.md:24` \u2014 the scanner is itself invoked via `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` inside a fence that is the instruction, not an illustration. These are Claude-Code-only forms (see `CLAIMS-REGISTER.md` entry 2) and are exempt from the scanner (#3445).\\n\\nStale description after the `docs/` deletion:\\n\\n- `skills/plugin-creator-meta-docs/SKILL.md:3` advertises \\\"plugin validation error codes, skill creation, agent creation, or plugin structure\\\", but its `find ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs` index now lists one file, `skill-subdirectory-warning.md`, which covers none of those.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: the plugin that teaches the rule ships text that fails it, and `/plugin-creator:lint` reports it clean, so an installed consumer hits a file-not-found on `plugin-lifecycle` Phase 4 while the file two hundred lines earlier told it every path is bundled.\\n\\nWhat needs deciding: whether each line becomes a relative path, an inlined instruction, or (for the Claude-Code-only variable forms) stays as-is with the plugin declared Claude-Code-targeted \u2014 the same question #3445 leaves open for the scanner. The meta-docs description should describe what the index actually lists.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review of dab51da, session 0123saEQFTYnFb79CLozrH7i (2026-09-06)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n- **Related**: #3445 (scanner exemption), #3429, #3430\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"33dce988dc87ff6f29d7d452d627f3f99631b983915ffd03d618c2c2141038f3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIymZQ\"}"}